      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="His embarrassment explains why he avoided the message, but he still accepts responsibility for not warning Nora." data-hint="The record explicitly says the explanation did not remove the impact." data-fix="His embarrassment explains why he avoided the message, but he still accepts responsibility for not warning Nora."><p class="quiz-question">2. How does the record treat Eli’s explanation?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="His embarrassment explains why he avoided the message, but he still accepts responsibility for not warning Nora.">His embarrassment explains why he avoided the message, but he still accepts responsibility for not warning Nora.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="His embarrassment proves Nora experienced no impact.">His embarrassment proves Nora experienced no impact.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The explanation transfers all responsibility to the client.">The explanation transfers all responsibility to the client.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="Send a risk update by 3:00 p.m. when a deadline is in danger." data-hint="Choose the action Nora asks Eli to perform." data-fix="Nora requests a risk update by 3:00 p.m. when a deadline is in danger."><p class="quiz-question">3. What specific request does Nora make?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Send a risk update by 3:00 p.m. when a deadline is in danger.">Send a risk update by 3:00 p.m. when a deadline is in danger.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Never experience embarrassment during any project.">Never experience embarrassment during any project.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Guarantee that no future deadline can ever change.">Guarantee that no future deadline can ever change.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="Nora does not answer project messages after 8:00 p.m. and replies the next morning." data-hint="Choose the sentence about Nora’s own availability and action." data-fix="Nora does not answer project messages after 8:00 p.m. and replies the next morning."><p class="quiz-question">4. What boundary does Nora state?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Nora does not answer project messages after 8:00 p.m. and replies the next morning.">Nora does not answer project messages after 8:00 p.m. and replies the next morning.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Eli is forbidden to think about work after 8:00 p.m.">Eli is forbidden to think about work after 8:00 p.m.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Every coworker must use the same availability in all workplaces.">Every coworker must use the same availability in all workplaces.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="Eli sent every agreed status and risk message for three weeks." data-hint="Choose the later repeated behavior, not the apology sentence alone." data-fix="Eli sent every agreed status and risk message for the next three weeks."><p class="quiz-question">5. What evidence supports saying that trust was beginning to rebuild?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Eli sent every agreed status and risk message for three weeks.">Eli sent every agreed status and risk message for three weeks.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Eli used the word sorry once, so trust instantly returned completely.">Eli used the word sorry once, so trust instantly returned completely.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Nora forgot that the late plan had ever existed.">Nora forgot that the late plan had ever existed.</button></div></div>
